From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lusoris <lusoris@proton.me>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 23:43:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] avfilter/vf_tonemap: add dynamic peak detection

The new peak_detect option measures the signal peak of every frame
instead of taking it from the peak option or the side data. The
detector follows libplacebo v7.360.1: the luminance is PQ-encoded at
14 bits over 16x16 tiles, the frame peak is the 99.995th percentile of
the histogram, and the result is smoothed over about 20 frames. The
threshold option sets the scene change window, which blends from
smoothing to a reset between 5 and 15 times its value in percent of the
average PQ level; the default 0.2 is libplacebo's window of 1 to 3
percent.

A frame that carries lavfi.dovi.l1_max_pq from dovi_reshape is not
measured; its Dolby Vision level 1 peak is used instead, which is what
libplacebo does with the RPU. With peak_detect left at 0 the output is
unchanged.

The frame-independent parts, the percentile, the smoothing and the
level 1 lookup, live in the new tonemap_peak.c so that a hardware tone
map filter can share them; the per-pixel tile code stays in vf_tonemap.c.

Signed-off-by: lusoris <lusoris@proton.me>
